{'symbol': 'DISH', 'date': '2019-11-07 10:30:00', 'title': 'Dish Network Corp - Board Of Directors Has Approved A Proposed Rights Offering To Raise Proceeds Of Approximately $1 Billion', 'text': "DISH NETWORK ANNOUNCES RIGHTS OFFERING.DISH NETWORK CORP - BOARD OF DIRECTORS HAS APPROVED A PROPOSED RIGHTS OFFERING TO RAISE PROCEEDS OF APPROXIMATELY $1 BILLION.DISH NETWORK CORP - SUBSCRIPTION PRICE WILL BE $33.52 PER SHARE OF CLASS A COMMON STOCK.DISH NETWORK CORP - RIGHTS OFFERING WILL NOT PROVIDE FOR OVER-SUBSCRIPTION RIGHTS.DISH NETWORK CORP - SUBSCRIPTION RIGHTS WILL ENTITLE HOLDER TO ACQUIRE NEWLY-ISSUED SHARES OF DISH'S CLASS A COMMON STOCK."}
{'symbol': 'DISH', 'date': '2019-11-07 22:30:00', 'title': 'DISH Network Corporation Appoints Marc Rouanne and Stephen Bye to its Executive Team', 'text': "DISH Network Corporation announced that it has named wireless industry innovators Marc Rouanne and Stephen Bye to its executive wireless leadership team. Rouanne will serve as Chief Network Officer and Bye will serve as Chief Commercial Officer. Both will join DISH as executive vice presidents and report to DISH Co-Founder and Chairman Charlie Ergen. As Chief Network Officer, Rouanne will oversee the strategy and architecture of the network, its core, and its cloud and edge strategies. Bye, most recently CEO of Connectivity Wireless, is a 28-year veteran of telecommunications and wireless who served as President of C-Spire and CTO of Sprint. He will lead the DISH wireless enterprise development team. The team's mission is to define, develop and market commercial applications, as well as establish strategic enterprise partnerships that are able to harness the unique architecture of DISH's software-defined 5G broadband network."}
